	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## AI Dashboard

Browse local **Claude Code** and **Codex** sessions, usage and limits. Type `aidash` (or the keyword you set below), or `aidash demo` to see sample data (`aidash demo archived` opens the sample archive). Sample data is invented and safe to screenshot.

### Requirements

- Alfred 6 with the Powerpack
- `python3` for the dashboard (install Apple's Command Line Tools with `xcode-select --install` if you do not have it)
- Claude Code and/or Codex, used at least once. Turn off the one you do not use.
- Optional: `tmux`; `zstd` to preview older Codex sessions that Codex compressed

### Using it

- Select a session to preview its latest messages. Press Return or double-click to resume it in your terminal, in tmux if you use it.
- A separate window matches your Alfred theme's light or dark look.
- Right-click for more actions. ⌘1 / ⌘2 / ⌘3 filter, ⌘4 shows archived sessions, ⌘R refreshes.
- **Archive** asks first. The archived view offers **Restore** and **Delete…**. Claude Code sessions are archived to `ai-dashboard-archive` inside the Claude folder; Codex uses `codex archive`.
- **Delete Permanently** cannot be undone. Open sessions cannot be archived or deleted.

### Claude Code limits

Claude Code gives its limits to the status line. In Claude Code, use `/statusline` to set it up:

`/statusline keep my status line as it is, and when rate_limits is present save that object to ~/.claude/ai-dashboard-rate-limits.json`

Until then, the dashboard shows the figures Claude Code last cached in `~/.claude.json`, which can be hours old. The newer reading is used, with its time.

### Privacy

Everything is read from local folders (`~/.claude` and `~/.codex` unless changed). Nothing is sent anywhere. From `~/.claude.json` only the cached usage figures are used. Titles and short message excerpts are cached in the workflow's cache folder. Turn previews off to keep message text out of it; generated titles are still cached. Token figures are uncached input plus output counted from local logs, not billing figures.

### Configuration

Choose the tools shown, their data folders, terminal and tmux behaviour, list and preview size, limit wording, refresh rate, resume options, and whether permanent deletion is allowed.
